{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "The six candidate models from PROJECT.md 8.1, with the facts the fit",
    "estimator needs. Data, not code, because these are report numbers: they",
    "get checked, corrected and cited, and that should never require a commit",
    "to a Python module.",
    "",
    "Every declared number carries `source` and `verified`. `verified: false`",
    "means nobody has checked it against the model card yet \u2014 the API passes",
    "that through and the UI marks it, so an unchecked figure can never be",
    "mistaken for a confirmed one on its way into the report.",
    "",
    "Declared values are only ever placeholders. The moment a model is pulled,",
    "Ollama's /api/show reports its real architecture and /api/tags its real",
    "size on disk, and services/model_fit.py prefers those. See MODULES.md 2.2:",
    "an estimate and a measurement must never look alike.",
    "",
    "Two sets in one list. `shortlist: true` marks the six candidates from",
    "PROJECT.md 8.1 that the report argues about; the rest are the wider Ollama",
    "library, present so the console can answer 'what else could this machine",
    "run?'. Library entries carry no MMLU on purpose \u2014 inventing quality scores",
    "for thirty models is the fabrication the shortlist's verified flags exist",
    "to prevent, and they score on fit and speed instead.",
    "",
    "Every tag here was verified against registry.ollama.ai. services/",
    "ollama_registry.py re-checks them at runtime and also reads each tag's real",
    "weight size from its manifest, which replaces the params x bytes/param",
    "arithmetic before anything is downloaded."
  ],
